.TH SESSLINT-CHECK 1 "" "SessLint 0.4.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-check \- [read\-only] Check a session file with auto\-detection.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint check [\-\-format {auto,claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}] [\-\-profile PROFILE] [\-\-policy CHECK_POLICY] [\-\-recursive | \-r] [\-\-follow\-symlinks] [\-\-max\-files MAX_FILES] [\-\-max\-bytes MAX_BYTES] [\-\-json] [\-\-output\-format {human,json,sarif,html}] [\-\-progress\-json] [\-\-color {auto,always,never}] [\-\-no\-color] [\-\-confidence\-min CONFIDENCE_MIN] [\-\-margin\-min MARGIN_MIN] [\-\-skip\-undetected] [\-\-fail\-on {error,warning}] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-select CODES] [\-\-ignore CODES] [\-\-baseline PATH] [\-\-write\-baseline PATH] [\-\-exclude GLOB] [\-\-ext EXT] [\-\-include\-content] [\-\-seal LEDGER] [\-\-seal\-no\-path] [\-\-seal\-genesis\-of HEX] PATH...
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Check a session file for structural defects, causal breaks, and schema violations.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B PATH
Path(s) to session file(s) (.json or .jsonl) or directories. Multiple paths produce one aggregated scan report. '\-' reads one session artifact from stdin (max 100 MB).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-format {auto,claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}
Session format adapter (default: auto) Choices: auto, claude\-code\-jsonl, openai\-agents, codex\-rollout, canonical.
.TP
.B \-\-profile PROFILE
Replay validation profile (default: neutral)
.TP
.B \-\-policy CHECK_POLICY
[Invalid for check] Repair policy is only applicable to 'repair'
.TP
.B \-\-recursive, \-r
Recursively scan directory trees for session artifacts
.TP
.B \-\-follow\-symlinks
[lossy: follows links] Follow directory symlinks during recursive scanning
.TP
.B \-\-max\-files MAX_FILES
Maximum number of files to inspect during recursive scan (default: 10000)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-bytes MAX_BYTES
Maximum cumulative bytes to read during recursive scan (default: 1GB)
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output check report as a single canonical JSON document to stdout
.TP
.B \-\-output\-format {human,json,sarif,html}
Output format (default: human; \-\-json is equivalent to 'json') Choices: human, json, sarif, html.
.TP
.B \-\-progress\-json
Emit NDJSON progress events to stderr (stdout stays the result channel)
.TP
.B \-\-color {auto,always,never}
Control colored output in human report mode (default: auto) Choices: auto, always, never.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color styling
.TP
.B \-\-confidence\-min CONFIDENCE_MIN
Format auto\-detection minimum confidence threshold
.TP
.B \-\-margin\-min MARGIN_MIN
Format auto\-detection minimum margin threshold
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-undetected
Classify files whose format cannot be detected as skipped instead of invalid (useful for pre\-commit hooks and mixed\-content trees)
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on {error,warning}
Minimum finding severity that fails the command (default: error) Choices: error, warning.
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
Explicit config file path (overrides [tool.sesslint] discovery)
.TP
.B \-\-select CODES
Comma\-separated rule codes to run exclusively (e.g. SL101,SL102)
.TP
.B \-\-ignore CODES
Comma\-separated rule codes to skip (e.g. SL101,SL102)
.TP
.B \-\-baseline PATH
Suppress findings whose fingerprints are recorded in baseline file
.TP
.B \-\-write\-baseline PATH
Write the current finding fingerprints as a new baseline file
.TP
.B \-\-exclude GLOB
Skip files/dirs whose name or root\-relative path matches GLOB (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-\-ext EXT
Only inspect files with these extensions during directory walks (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-\-include\-content
Embed raw transcript content in reports (warning: emits raw sensitive data)
.TP
.B \-\-seal LEDGER
Append a tamper\-evident seal line to LEDGER (append\-only hash\-chained verdict record; 'sesslint seal \-\-verify' re\-checks it)
.TP
.B \-\-seal\-no\-path
Omit the artifact path from the seal line (multi\-machine ledgers)
.TP
.B \-\-seal\-genesis\-of HEX
Bind a new ledger's first line to a prior ledger's last entry hash (ledger rotation)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — clean check, or repair executed, validated, and manifested.
.TP
.B 1
Finding / refusal — diagnostic errors found, repair plan blocked, or
execution refused (TOCTOU, SL203).
.TP
.B 2
Operational error — CLI syntax error, file not found, permission denied,
or live-DB path refusal.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-baseline(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-completion(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

